A dramatic aerial view of a vast ocean with a small wooden sailing ship navigating through swirling, spiral-shaped currents and waves that form concentric circular patterns in the deep blue water. The currents create natural pathways radiating outward from a central calm eye, with some waves zooming into detailed whitecaps while others fade into the broader seascape. Schools of fish follow curved trajectories beneath the translucent surface. The perspective shifts dynamically, showing both the macro view of the entire spiral ocean system and micro details of the weathered ship deck. Dramatic storm clouds part to reveal golden sunlight illuminating specific sections of the water's path. Style: Vincent van Gogh with bold, expressive brushstrokes creating movement in every wave, swirling skies reminiscent of Starry Night, rich impasto texture in deep teals, cerulean blues, and touches of amber light.
